  "_doc": "The baseline archive: every model SkippyCore, Skippy's voice and the fallback plan may want, downloaded once into MODELS_ROOT (D:\\models) by tools/models_baseline.py (the midnight task: tools/install_models_baseline_task.sh). Each entry is a Hugging Face repo (NVIDIA's open speech models live there too) with optional include/ignore globs, or a direct url. Order matters: 'core' downloads first, 'extended' fills the disk after it, and the run stops before free space drops under the reserve. A repo that finished is never re-downloaded (its SOURCE.json says complete), so the archive stays the baseline even when the repo changes upstream. approx_gb is what the globs select, rounded (2026-10-16 listings). Licences travel in each SOURCE.json; several are non-commercial: personal use only.",
